<title>UK: Reuters 3rd UK-Americas/Africa/Nordic air cargo report.</title>
<headline>Reuters 3rd UK-Americas/Africa/Nordic air cargo report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>This is Reuters 3rd ex-UK air cargo market rates report covering the America, Africa and the Nordic countries. The linked market report has been divided into one covering the Americas and one for Africa and Europe.</p>
<p>This report and one covering the ex-UK market to Asia/Australasia/MidEast are issued on alternate weeks.</p>
<p>Below are the current average ex-UK air cargo rates to the United States, Latin America, Africa and Scandinavia per kg for a 100 kg shipment, with a volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-one.</p>
<p>		   March 14	  March 3</p>
<p>		  UNITED STATES</p>
<p> LON-JFK	 0.64		0.63</p>
<p> LON-LAX	 0.82		0.80</p>
<p> LON-CHI	 0.77		0.74</p>
<p>		  LATIN AMERICA</p>
<p> LON-SAO	 2.08		2.10</p>
<p> LON-BUE	 2.21		2.21</p>
<p>		  AFRICA</p>
<p> LON-JNB	 1.63		1.63</p>
<p> LON-NBO	 0.94		0.93</p>
<p>		  SCANDINAVIA</p>
<p> LON-STO	 0.74		0.73</p>
<p> LON-CPH	 0.68		0.70</p>
<p>*The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters journalists on a confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents at the three main London airports.</p>
<p>*All prices are quoted in sterling.</p>
<p>*The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices and are indicative of current market activity.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax: 5017</p>
</text>
